{
  peppy_schema: "contract/v1",
  manifest: {
    name: "scene_materials",
    tag: "v1",
    description: [
      "The optical properties of the materials in a simulated scene, edited while the simulation runs: discover the materials, read their effective values, set the colour or the finish of one, and restore the authored values.",
      "A material is shared: every surface that references it changes together, and get_materials states that scope for each one, so a caller knows what an edit reaches before making it. A change shows up in every view the engine renders, the robot's cameras included; it never recompiles the scene and never touches mass, friction or collision.",
      "Material ids are stable for the life of a loaded scene and come from get_materials. Colour is the base reflectance, linear RGB in the unit interval; metallic and roughness are the unit-interval parameters of the metallic-roughness model (0 metallic is a dielectric, 1 a conductor; 0 roughness a mirror finish, 1 fully diffuse). A setter validates its whole request before it changes anything: it gives an error reply with `rejected` to a request for an unknown material, or with a value out of the unit interval or not finite, and the material stays as it was. The response of a setter gives the effective values after the call.",
      "Loading or clearing a scene through scene_manipulation restores the authored materials; reset_materials does the same for what is loaded.",
    ],
  },
  interfaces: {
    services: [
      {
        name: "get_materials",
        description: "Give every editable material, as a JSON object in materials_json. An engine that has no materials to report, because no scene is loaded yet, gives an error reply with `precondition_failed`.",
        response_message_format: {
          materials_json: {
            $type: "string",
            $description: "Every editable material as a JSON object: {\"materials\": [...]}. Each material carries \"id\", \"label\", \"scope\" ({\"owner\": \"<robot instance or scene>\", \"surfaces\": <count of surfaces sharing it>, \"bodies\": [<body names>]}) and \"properties\", an object with \"color_rgb\", \"metallic\" and \"roughness\", each with \"unit\", \"default\" and \"value\" (and \"min\", \"max\" for the scalars).",
          },
        },
      },
      {
        name: "set_material_color",
        description: "Set the material's base colour, linear RGB reflectance in the unit interval.",
        request_message_format: {
          material_id: "string",
          color: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3 },
        },
        response_message_format: {
          current_color: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3 },
        },
      },
      {
        name: "set_material_finish",
        description: "Set the material's finish: metallic and roughness, both in the unit interval, checked together and applied together.",
        request_message_format: {
          material_id: "string",
          metallic: "f64",
          roughness: "f64",
        },
        response_message_format: {
          current_metallic: "f64",
          current_roughness: "f64",
        },
      },
      {
        name: "reset_materials",
        description: "Put every material back to its authored values.",
      },
    ],
  },
}
